1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:05,000
Every evening, millions of journeys light up Dhaka.

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:10,200
This is চলো — built for how Bangladesh really moves.

3
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:21,400
A walkthrough of the whole platform — the real app first, then the next generation.

4
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:29,300
Everything starts on cholo-cholo7.vercel.app.

5
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:33,550
The home page tells one ride, step by step — from booking to rating.

6
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:40,000
On a phone, swipe through all eleven moments of a চলো ride.

7
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:46,050
Book, match, women-only, arrive, board, ride, detour, pay, rate, Metro and the digital twin.

8
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:55,050
Dark mode, and a fully Bangla interface — every screen, every label.

9
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:04,550
Create an account with your phone number. A six-digit code arrives by SMS.

10
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:10,000
Type where you’re going — suggestions appear as you type.

11
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:14,550
The route is drawn on real roads. Need a stop on the way? Add it.

12
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:22,550
Every vehicle shows its fare before you book. No haggling, no surprises.

13
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:31,050
Add a promo code, schedule for tomorrow morning, or ask for a woman driver.

14
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:36,600
Nusrat confirms. Rahim’s phone lights up with the offer: ৳182, 7.2 km.

15
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:41,550
He accepts — and Nusrat sees her driver straight away.

16
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:49,050
Rahim drives to the pickup. Every move shows live on Nusrat’s map.

17
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:53,400
Rahim slides “I’ve arrived”. But the trip can’t start yet.

18
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:58,100
If he isn’t really there, Nusrat taps “My driver isn’t here” — and he’s sent back.

19
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:02,800
When he’s truly at the pickup, Nusrat confirms she’s in the car.

20
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:05,550
Only then can the trip start. No fake pickups, ever.

21
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:10,300
Nusrat taps “Share trip”. The link is copied.

22
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:16,550
Ammu opens it at home: the CNG, the driver, the plate and the ETA — all live.

23
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:23,300
Feel unsafe? The red SOS button is always on the trip screen.

24
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:31,050
One tap: Cholo auto-calls your SOS contact and 999, and sends your live location to family.

25
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:35,800
Tap SOS and Cholo instantly places an automated call to your saved SOS contact.

26
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:40,600
A voice reads out where you are — the street, the landmark, the car and its plate.

27
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:45,500
At the same moment, 999 gets an automated call with your exact live location.

28
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:51,300
Nusrat wants to get out early. She taps “Stop here”.

29
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:56,550
Rahim ends the trip where they are — and the fare covers only the distance driven.

30
00:02:57,100 --> 00:03:02,900
Nusrat chose bKash. She’s taken to the secure checkout.

31
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:07,550
Account number, PIN, confirm — paid. Rahim’s earnings land in his wallet.

32
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:15,050
A clear receipt for every trip. Five stars for Rahim — and he’s a favourite now.

33
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:23,050
Trip history, wallet top-ups, promos, inbox and saved places — all one tap away.

34
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:30,600
Any rider can apply to drive: NID, licence number and expiry date.

35
00:03:30,700 --> 00:03:34,550
An expired licence or document is rejected on the spot, before it ever reaches review.

36
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:39,100
Rahim’s green CNG is approved and on duty. He goes online.

37
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:45,550
A ride offer slides in — fare, distance, pickup — with fourteen seconds to accept.

38
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:51,300
Farhana drives for Cholo. One switch turns on “Women riders only”.

39
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:57,550
Every offer she gets is from a verified woman rider — requests from men never reach her.

40
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:03,100
She picks her own hours and gets paid every day, straight to her own bKash.

41
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:08,550
Earning on her own terms and feeling safe in Dhaka is still rare. Cholo makes it normal.

42
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:17,550
Rahim earned ৳5,064 in thirty days. Every trip and every commission is listed.

43
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:23,550
A statement for every month: trips, fares, the 15% commission and what he kept.

44
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:31,050
Rahim withdraws ৳2,000 to his bKash. He can follow it in his history.

45
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:41,550
The operations dashboard: today’s trips, drivers, revenue and live SOS — per city or all.

46
00:04:42,100 --> 00:04:48,062
Monthly revenue, where the money goes, busiest hours, best days, top drivers and riders.

47
00:04:48,612 --> 00:04:55,182
The commissions report: search any date range or city for rides, ride cost and commission earned.

48
00:04:55,732 --> 00:05:01,098
Review each licence, NID and photo — then approve the driver or vehicle in one click.

49
00:05:01,648 --> 00:05:05,148
Zones for every city: regular areas, airports, stations and restricted no-go areas.

50
00:05:05,248 --> 00:05:08,598
Draw a new zone right on the map — it’s live the moment you save.

51
00:05:09,148 --> 00:05:14,382
Driver withdrawals wait for finance: approve to send, or reject with a reason.

52
00:05:14,932 --> 00:05:20,882
Effective-dated rate cards for every city and vehicle, and surge you can start or end per zone.

53
00:05:21,432 --> 00:05:27,382
The SOS board shows live alerts on a map. Disputes and refunds are handled in one queue.

54
00:05:27,932 --> 00:05:33,882
Support tickets for every rider and driver — and an audit log no one can edit or delete.

55
00:05:36,632 --> 00:05:39,832
Everything you’ve seen is live. Now meet the intelligence behind চলো.

56
00:05:40,432 --> 00:05:46,032
The Dhaka Digital Twin: 5,000 simulated drivers and riders on the real road network.

57
00:05:46,232 --> 00:05:50,882
Every algorithm is tested here first — the new dispatch cuts pickup time by 22%.

58
00:05:51,432 --> 00:05:56,032
Cholo Maps: our own vector map, with Bangla labels and 3D buildings.

59
00:05:56,232 --> 00:06:00,382
Every driver’s GPS becomes a traffic probe — the Cholo Traffic Layer, live.

60
00:06:00,932 --> 00:06:04,732
Drop a pin inside a building and Cholo moves it to the gate riders actually use.

61
00:06:04,832 --> 00:06:08,232
Driver GPS traces reveal roads the map is missing — and Cholo adds them.

62
00:06:08,932 --> 00:06:16,232
At a crowded pickup, AR arrows lead you to your CNG — and the camera reads its Bangla plate.

63
00:06:16,932 --> 00:06:22,132
“Mirpur 10 golchottor er pashe, Shopno er samne” — Cholo finds exactly that spot.

64
00:06:22,332 --> 00:06:25,382
Gulshan, gulsan, গুলশান or gulshun — every spelling lands in the same place.

65
00:06:25,932 --> 00:06:28,532
“Hospital with emergency open now” — results ranked by what’s open.

66
00:06:28,632 --> 00:06:31,132
At 8:45 on a weekday, Office is already waiting, priced and one tap away.

67
00:06:31,232 --> 00:06:33,382
Cholo Codes: a short code with the gate photo, exact pin and a voice note for the driver.

68
00:06:33,932 --> 00:06:38,532
“আমাকে এখন বনানী নিয়ে যাও, সস্তা দেখে” — take me to Banani now, the cheap option.

69
00:06:38,632 --> 00:06:42,882
The agent finds the cheapest ride, reads back the fare, and books it when you say yes.

70
00:06:43,432 --> 00:06:51,382
Book on WhatsApp, Messenger or SMS — or dial *CHOLO# on any basic phone, no internet needed.

71
00:06:51,932 --> 00:06:55,532
Drivers keep both hands on the wheel: “Accept”, “I’ve arrived” — done by voice.

72
00:06:55,632 --> 00:06:59,382
A tourist types in English, Rahim reads Bangla — and replies, translated back instantly.

73
00:06:59,932 --> 00:07:03,932
“I was overcharged.” The agent replays the GPS trace and finds a 2.4 km detour.

74
00:07:04,032 --> 00:07:07,882
Within policy, it refunds ৳60 by itself — and every action goes into the audit log.

75
00:07:08,432 --> 00:07:16,382
“Why did cancellations spike in Uttara?” Cholo writes the SQL, draws the chart, explains.

76
00:07:16,932 --> 00:07:20,932
Nearest-driver dispatch makes some riders wait far too long.

77
00:07:21,032 --> 00:07:25,232
Batched matching solves for everyone at once — total waiting drops by a third.

78
00:07:25,932 --> 00:07:30,032
Cholo forecasts demand for every hexagon of Dhaka — 15, 30 and 60 minutes ahead.

79
00:07:30,132 --> 00:07:34,232
Idle drivers are told where to go before the rush, so riders wait less and drivers earn more.

80
00:07:34,932 --> 00:07:38,532
When prices rise, Cholo says why — and surge is smooth between areas and always capped.

81
00:07:38,632 --> 00:07:42,232
ETAs are learned from real trips, so “5 minutes” really means five minutes.

82
00:07:42,932 --> 00:07:45,732
Cholo Pool: two riders going the same way share one car and each pays less.

83
00:07:45,832 --> 00:07:48,632
Add three stops and Cholo puts them in the fastest order — one fare.

84
00:07:48,732 --> 00:07:51,232
And the upfront fare is guaranteed, whatever the traffic does.

85
00:07:51,932 --> 00:07:59,232
See Dhaka’s peak hours, lock a fare for ten minutes, and get pinged when your route gets cheaper.

86
00:07:59,932 --> 00:08:03,532
Monsoon rain: when the fleet slows to a crawl and drivers tap “water here”, Cholo knows.

87
00:08:03,632 --> 00:08:08,232
Routes re-draw around waterlogged roads, so you arrive a little later — but never stuck.

88
00:08:08,932 --> 00:08:11,532
Uttara to Motijheel at rush hour. A car takes 55 minutes and ৳320.

89
00:08:11,632 --> 00:08:18,132
Cholo plans it smarter: a bike to Uttara North, then MRT Line 6 straight across the city.

90
00:08:18,232 --> 00:08:22,382
A short walk and you’re there — 25 minutes sooner, for less than half the price.

91
00:08:22,932 --> 00:08:25,932
A fair-fare meter for street CNGs. Women-safe night routes with women drivers.

92
00:08:26,032 --> 00:08:31,382
Eid mode for the exodus, and a Lite mode that books a ride over a 2G connection.

93
00:08:31,932 --> 00:08:35,932
If a car leaves its route or stops for too long, Cholo checks in. No answer? It escalates.

94
00:08:36,032 --> 00:08:39,882
A sudden crash shows up in the phone’s motion sensors — help is called automatically.

95
00:08:40,432 --> 00:08:43,032
An on-device camera model spots tired eyes and tells the driver to rest.

96
00:08:43,132 --> 00:08:45,732
A selfie liveness check at every shift stops account sharing.

97
00:08:45,832 --> 00:08:48,232
And a weekly driving score rewards the safest drivers.

98
00:08:48,932 --> 00:08:56,232
A graph of users, devices and wallets exposes fake trips and spoofed GPS.

99
00:08:56,932 --> 00:09:04,232
Earnings forecasts, a shift planner, true profit after fuel, an EV calculator and instant document scans.

100
00:09:04,932 --> 00:09:12,732
Animated trip recaps, a yearly Cholo Wrapped, lock-screen progress — and accessibility built in.

101
00:09:13,432 --> 00:09:21,232
Every ping streamed, matching in two seconds, and anonymised insights for the city.

102
00:09:21,932 --> 00:09:28,232
Parcels, food, airport rides, business accounts, rewards, EV fleets — one platform for all of it.

103
00:09:31,932 --> 00:09:38,732
Everything a city needs to move — in one app.

104
00:09:42,432 --> 00:09:47,632
Cholo runs on a lean, serverless stack — open maps, no licence fees, and you pay as you grow.

105
00:09:47,732 --> 00:09:53,382
Launch for about ৳6,300 a month instead of lakhs. No map bills, no servers to babysit.

106
00:09:53,932 --> 00:09:59,132
Why start up with Cholo? Rider, driver and admin apps, payments, safety and AI are all built.

107
00:09:59,232 --> 00:10:04,382
Open a new city in a day: draw the zones, set the rate card, approve drivers — and go live.

108
00:10:04,932 --> 00:10:10,432
Cholo versus Uber: drivers keep more — 15% commission instead of around 25%.

109
00:10:10,532 --> 00:10:16,382
Women-only matching, SOS auto-calls, Metro and flood routing — and profits stay in Bangladesh.

110
00:10:16,932 --> 00:10:22,432
Revenue from day one: 15% on every trip, plus deliveries, business accounts and partner promos.

111
00:10:22,532 --> 00:10:28,882
Just 1,000 drivers doing 12 trips a day brings in about ৳97 lakh a month, on a ৳6,300 stack.

112
00:10:29,432 --> 00:10:37,232
Ready to launch, cheap to run, built for Bangladesh. Cholo is the startup Dhaka is waiting for.

